<div class="container ag">

<h1 id="top">Autonomous Agents (job-specific) — Incorporation Plan</h1>

<div class="last-updated" style="color: var(--text-muted-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">
    Created: 2026-08-15 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Version: 1.0 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Status: PLANNING &nbsp;|&nbsp;
    Project: <a href="/project/details?project_id=267">#267 AGENTS</a>
</div>

<p>This plan answers one question: <strong>how do we bring the outskill.com "Claude &amp; AI Mastermind" idea —
independent agents that each do a specific job — into Comserv2?</strong> The good news: the foundation already
exists. We do <em>not</em> start from scratch. The AI2 subsystem already has a model/provider router, a
provider abstraction (Ollama / Grok / OpenRouter), and a purpose-built <code>/ai2/token-login</code> endpoint
described in its own source as the "agent/test harness login". This plan wraps that into a first-class,
observable <strong>agent framework</strong> and then ships a first wave of concrete <strong>job agents</strong>.</p>

<div class="notice">
    <strong>Reuse, do not duplicate.</strong> Two prior designs already exist and are folded in here, not
    rewritten:
    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/ai_workflows/DailyPlanAutomatorDesign') %]">Daily Plan Automator Design</a>
    (the 4-agent Audit &rarr; DocsSync &rarr; MasterPlanUpdater &rarr; DailyPlansGenerator pipeline) becomes the
    flagship job agent; and
    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/ai_workflows/docker-agent-guide') %]">Docker Agent guide</a> shows the
    existing agent-spec pattern. This plan promotes that into a real runtime.
</div>

<p class="back-to-top"><a href="/planning/daily#master-plan">&#8592; Back to Daily Plan &middot; MASTER PLAN</a></p>

