<div class="card" id="concept"><details open><summary class="card-header">1. The concept (from the seminar)</summary>
<div class="card-body">
<p>The outskill.com "Claude &amp; AI Mastermind" session is about <strong>independent agents that each own one
specific job</strong> — not one giant chatbot, but small, purpose-built workers that run on a trigger, do their
task against real tools/data, and report back. Translate that to Comserv2 vocabulary:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Agent</strong> = a named, registered worker with one job (e.g. "Daily Audit", "Docs Sync", "DB Drift Guard", "Email Triage").</li>
    <li><strong>Job</strong> = a deterministic procedure the agent executes: inputs &rarr; tool calls &rarr; outputs written back to the app (DB rows, docs, todos, files).</li>
    <li><strong>Trigger</strong> = schedule (cron), event (todo closed, deploy finished), or manual (button / API).</li>
    <li><strong>Gateway</strong> = the agent authenticates as a real app identity (via the existing <code>/ai2/token-login</code>) and is confined to scoped tools — never a raw shell.</li>
    <li><strong>Observability</strong> = every run is a logged record: what it did, which model/provider it used, tokens/cost, and pass/fail.</li>
</ul>
<p>This is exactly the shape of the Daily Plan Automator's 4-agent pipeline, generalised.</p>
</div>
</details></div>

<div class="card" id="grounding"><details><summary class="card-header">2. What already exists (grounding — do not rebuild)</summary>
<div class="card-body">
<table class="data-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Where</th><th>What it gives the agent system</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>AI2 Router</td><td><code>lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/Router.pm</code></td><td>Single brain that picks provider+model per context/role. <code>dispatch_chat()</code> is the one place every agent should send chat — already used by chat widget, Git drafting, Focus-Tune.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Provider layer</td><td><code>Model/AI2/Provider/{Ollama,Grok,OpenRouter}.pm</code></td><td>Local-first (free) + external (paid) chat clients. Agent cost stays at zero by preferring Ollama.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Agent gateway</td><td><code>Controller/AI2.pm :: token_login</code> (line ~471)</td><td>Purpose-built <code>/ai2/token-login</code>: exchanges an <code>ApiToken</code> for a real authenticated Catalyst session so a CLI/agent "acts as the user". This is the agent auth path — reuse it.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Diagnostics / test harness</td><td><code>Controller/AI2.pm :: diagnostics, test_model</code></td><td>Live "what is the system doing" snapshot persisted to <code>logs/ai2_diagnostics/</code>. Reuse as the agent run-record seed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Daily Plan Automator</td><td><code>root/Documentation/ai_workflows/DailyPlanAutomatorDesign.tt</code></td><td>Already-designed 4-agent pipeline. Becomes the first shipped job agent, not new design.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Project/Todo API</td><td><code>Controller/Api.pm</code> (<code>/api/project/create</code>, <code>/api/project/update</code>, <code>/api/projects</code>)</td><td>Agents create/update real projects &amp; todos; human reviews them. Local-network auth already in place.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Principle:</strong> agents talk to the app the same way the AI2 diagnostics harness already does — through
authenticated endpoints — and think through the Router. No new LLM plumbing.</p>
</div>
</details></div>

<div class="card" id="architecture"><details><summary class="card-header">3. Target architecture (thin, layered, reuse-first)</summary>
<div class="card-body">
<pre class="ag-pre">
                         ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   TRIGGER  (cron /      │            AGENT RUNTIME  (new, thin)          │
   event / API)  ───────▶│  Comserv::Model::AI2::Agent::*                 │
                         │   • Registry   (agent defs: job, tools, sched) │
                         │   • Runner      (spawn, call Router, capture)  │
                         │   • Sandbox     (scoped tool allow-list)       │
                         │   • RunLedger   (every run logged)             │
                         └───────┬───────────────────────┬────────────────┘
                                 │ thinks via            │ acts via
                                 ▼                        ▼
                    AI2::Router (dispatch_chat)   App endpoints (token-login session)
                    Ollama ▸ Grok ▸ OpenRouter     /api/projects, /api/todos, /Documentation,
                                                        schema-compare, git (whitelisted)
                                 │
                                 ▼
                    AGENT OPS (#270): run log + token/cost accounting + human-approval gate + kill-switch
</pre>
<p>Hard constraints carried from <code>.hermes.md</code> / <code>.ai-policy.md</code> (same as the Master Plan):</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>No app restart, no edit to <code>comserv_server.pl</code></strong> (Shanta owns lifecycle). Verify with <code>perl -c</code>, <code>node --check</code>, endpoint calls.</li>
    <li><strong>Schema rule:</strong> any new agent/run table goes through the in-app schema-compare workflow. Result class = source of truth. NEVER hand-write DDL.</li>
    <li><strong>One schema mechanism:</strong> all DB in <code>Util::SchemaCompare</code> + <code>Util::Schema::*</code>. Zero raw SQL in controllers.</li>
    <li><strong>JS:</strong> modular <code>static/js/</code> wired through <code>js_load.tt</code>, <code>data-*</code> delegation. No inline <code>&lt;script&gt;</code>. Theme via <code>var(--*)</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>No duplicate files; consolidate; stay in scope.</strong> Reuse the AI2 Router, not a second LLM path.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</details></div>

<div class="card" id="framework"><details><summary class="card-header">4. Phase (proj #268 AGENTS-CORE) — Generic Agent Framework</summary>
<div class="card-body">
<p><strong>Goal:</strong> a small, reusable runtime any job agent can plug into. Keep it &le;800 lines (Util/Model soft limit).</p>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Registry</strong> — <code>Model::AI2::Agent::Registry</code>. Agent definitions are rows (not code forks): <code>agent_jobs</code> table (code, name, description, job_class, trigger_type, schedule_cron, tool_allow_list, default_context, enabled). Defined via schema-compare.</li>
    <li><strong>Identity &amp; gateway reuse</strong> — agents authenticate through the existing <code>/ai2/token-login</code> (an <code>ApiToken</code> &rarr; Catalyst session). No new auth surface. Document the token-scoping contract.</li>
    <li><strong>Runner</strong> — <code>Model::AI2::Agent::Runner</code>. Loads a job, opens a token session, calls <code>Router-&gt;dispatch_chat</code> for reasoning, executes only allow-listed tools, writes outputs back via app endpoints, returns a structured result.</li>
    <li><strong>Sandbox / tool allow-list</strong> — every agent declares the tools it may call (e.g. <code>schema_compare</code>, <code>todo_write</code>, <code>doc_update</code>, <code>git_whitelisted</code>). Anything outside the list is denied by the Runner. Mirrors the existing <code>Util::Git</code> whitelisted-<code>git -C</code> runner pattern.</li>
    <li><strong>RunLedger</strong> — <code>agent_runs</code> table (agent_code, trigger, started, finished, status, model_used, provider, tokens_in, tokens_out, cost_usd, output_ref, error). Seed from the existing diagnostics snapshot format.</li>
</ol>
<div class="gate"><strong>Gate #268:</strong> one toy agent ("Echo/Self-test") runs end-to-end through the framework and writes a <code>agent_runs</code> row with zero code bypassing the Router.</div>
</div>
</details></div>

<div class="card" id="jobs"><details><summary class="card-header">5. Phase (proj #269 AGENTS-JOBS) — Built-in Job Agents (first wave)</summary>
<div class="card-body">
<p>Ship concrete agents on the framework. Each is one registered job + one tool allow-list. Reuse the Daily Plan
Automator design rather than re-deriving it.</p>
<table class="data-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Agent</th><th>Job</th><th>Tools (allow-list)</th><th>Trigger</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>Todo Create (in-chat)</td><td><strong>Code now</strong> (<code>Model::AI2::TodoCreate</code> + <code>Chat::process</code> intercept). Clear “add a todo …” does not use the picker. Absorb into Runner when #268 exists — do not rewrite. Tracking <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2217" title="Todo #2217 on #280.">#2217</a>.</td><td>todo_write, project_write</td><td>Chat widget / /ai/widget / editor chat</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Scheduler (queue order)</td><td><strong>Specified, not built</strong> (<a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2218" title="Opens todo #2218 on project #280 AISYSTEM.">#2218</a>). Blocker predecessor todos + start_date after remaining queue. Never bulk-rewrite every todo.</td><td>todo_write, todo_read, project_read</td><td>After Todo-create WRITE; Daily Plan; manual</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Daily Plan Automator</td><td>The existing 4-step pipeline (Audit &rarr; DocsSync &rarr; MasterPlanUpdater &rarr; DailyPlansGenerator), wired as one multi-step job.</td><td>todo_read, doc_read, doc_update, project_update, git_whitelisted</td><td>Schedule (early UTC)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Docs Sync</td><td>Map recent code/doc changes to <code>/Documentation/*.tt</code> and flag stale docs (ties to Doc Standard S1–S7).</td><td>doc_read, doc_update, git_whitelisted</td><td>Event (deploy finished) / schedule</td></tr>
        <tr><td>DB Drift Guard</td><td>Report-only schema drift vs Result classes; one-click repair via schema-compare. Ties to W0.1 (Schema System Plan).</td><td>schema_compare</td><td>Schedule (daily)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Email Triage</td><td>Summarise inbox, draft replies, create linked todos/projects. Reuses the email skill pattern.</td><td>todo_write, project_update, (read-only mail)</td><td>Schedule / manual</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p>Order: Daily Plan Automator first (design exists), then Docs Sync and DB Drift Guard (both read-mostly, low risk), then Email Triage (external surface, needs approval gate from #270).</p>
<div class="gate"><strong>Gate #269:</strong> Daily Plan Automator runs unattended against the live app and produces a verifiable <code>agent_runs</code> record + real (human-reviewable) doc/project changes.</div>
</div>
</details></div>

<div class="card" id="ops"><details><summary class="card-header">6. Phase (proj #270 AGENTS-OPS) — Agent Ops &amp; Safety</summary>
<div class="card-body">
<ul>
    <li><strong>Run log &amp; audit:</strong> every run persisted to <code>agent_runs</code>; surfaced in a thin <code>/admin/agents</code> view (reuse <code>container</code>/<code>data-table</code> theme). Wire into the existing error-audit pipeline (<code>Comserv::Util::Logging</code> only).</li>
    <li><strong>Cost / token accounting:</strong> aggregate <code>tokens_in/out</code> + <code>cost_usd</code> per agent per day from Router pricing (already carried by the catalog). Local Ollama = $0; external capped per the role tiers in <code>Router.pm</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Human-approval gate:</strong> agents that write externally-facing changes (Email Triage, anything that deploys) require a pending state + human "approve" before the write executes. Mirrors the git worktree human-audit gate.</li>
    <li><strong>Kill-switch:</strong> <code>agent_jobs.enabled = 0</code> stops a misbehaving agent; a global "pause all agents" flag in config. No app restart needed (Starman -r reloads).</li>
    <li><strong>Budget guard:</strong> hard daily token/$ ceiling per agent; over-budget runs fail closed and log.</li>
</ul>
<div class="gate"><strong>Gate #270:</strong> an agent pushed past its token budget fails closed, is visible in <code>/admin/agents</code>, and the event reaches the error-audit log.</div>
</div>
</details></div>

<div class="card" id="roadmap"><details><summary class="card-header">7. Sequencing / roadmap</summary>
<div class="card-body">
<pre class="ag-pre">
#268 AGENTS-CORE  ──┐  (framework: registry, gateway reuse, runner, sandbox, run-ledger)
                    ├──▶ #269 AGENTS-JOBS  (Daily Plan Automator first, then Docs Sync, Drift Guard, Email)
#270 AGENTS-OPS    ──┘  (ops can land in parallel once #268 RunLedger exists; gates enforced before JOBS writes go live)
</pre>
<p><strong>Dependency:</strong> #269 and #270 both depend on #268's RunLedger + gateway. #269's Email Triage depends on
#270's approval gate. Build order: #268 &rarr; #270 (minimal) &rarr; #269 (Automator) &rarr; remaining jobs &rarr; #270 full.</p>
<p><strong>Independent / parallelizable:</strong> DB Drift Guard (read-only, ties to W0.1) and Docs Sync can be built
as soon as #268 Runner exists.</p>
</div>
</details></div>

<div class="card" id="gates"><details><summary class="card-header">8. Done-when (gates recap)</summary>
<div class="card-body">
<ul>
    <li><strong>G1 (#268):</strong> toy agent runs end-to-end via the framework, writes an <code>agent_runs</code> row, uses only the Router for LLM calls.</li>
    <li><strong>G2 (#269):</strong> Daily Plan Automator runs unattended and produces verifiable, human-reviewable changes.</li>
    <li><strong>G3 (#270):</strong> budget breach fails closed + visible + audited.</li>
    <li><strong>G4 (all):</strong> no raw SQL in controllers, no app restart, theme via <code>var(--*)</code>, docs cross-linked from MASTER_PLAN.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</details></div>

